I see! When `partialDecoding = 0` (i.e., `decode_full_block`), the check `cpy > oend-MATCH_SAFEGUARD_DISTANCE` is skipped. And the code proceeds to copy the full match without checking if it fits in the output buffer.

But wait, there's a check earlier:
```c
if (unlikely(op+length > oend-LASTLITERALS)) {
    if (partialDecoding) length = MIN(length, (size_t)(oend-op));
    else goto _output_error;
}
```

If `partialDecoding = 0` and `op + length > oend - LASTLITERALS`, it goes to `_output_error`. So `op + length <= oend - LASTLITERALS < oend`. And `cpy = op + length <= oend - LASTLITERALS < oend`. So the copy is within bounds.

OK, so the `decode_full_block` path is safe too.

